      "summary": "Support video playback via libVLC (with fallback to built in player) (#1609)",
      "description": "* feat(vlc): integrate LibVLCSharp 4.x with VLC fallback to VideoPlayer\n\n- Add vlc-unity C# source (Assets/VLCUnity/) with graceful fallbacks\n- Add YargVideoPlayer wrapper: tries VLC, falls back to Unity VideoPlayer\n- VLCMediaPlayer: IsVLCAvailable flag, try-catch in Awake/Stop, Core.Initialize() fix for Linux\n- VLCUnityStubs: GetTexture extension stub (returns IntPtr.Zero)\n- BackgroundManager: use YargVideoPlayer, RequireComponent, Awake fallback\n- Timeout-based fallback: if VLC texture not available after 5s, switch to VideoPlayer\n- Wait for VideoPlayer.prepareCompleted before firing YargVideoPlayer.prepareCompleted\n- LibVLCSharp 4.0.0-alpha NuGet dependency (no native binaries included)\n\n* fix(vlc): call native libvlc_unity_get_texture via DllImport instead of stub\n\nThe VLCUnityStubs.cs extension method was intercepting player.GetTexture()\nand returning IntPtr.Zero, preventing the native VLCUnityPlugin from\ncapturing video frames. Now TextureHelper imports libvlc_unity_get_texture\ndirectly via DllImport, so VLC video renders to the render texture properly.\n\n* fix(vlc): use libvlc_unity_media_player_new for render context registration\n\nThe standard LibVLCSharp 4.x NuGet package creates MediaPlayer via\nlibvlc_media_player_new, which doesn't register in the VLCUnityPlugin's\ncontexts map. This causes libvlc_unity_get_texture to return null\n(video never captured to texture).\n\nFix: call libvlc_unity_media_player_new (which creates the media player\nAND registers it in the contexts map), then use reflection to replace\nthe MediaPlayer's NativeReference backing field since it's read-only\nin the NuGet package (private set in 3.x source).\n\nThis is necessary because vlc-unity uses a custom LibVLCSharp build\nthat has GetTexture and calls libvlc_unity_media_player_new, but we're\nusing the standard NuGet package.\n\n* refactor(vlc): use LibVLCSharp master branch with UNITY support\n\nReplaces the NuGet 4.x-alpha package with a build from the\nLibVLCSharp master branch, which has UNITY conditional compilation\nthat calls libvlc_unity_media_player_new and libvlc_unity_get_texture.\n\nThis eliminates all workarounds:\n- Removed DllImport for libvlc_unity_media_player_new + reflection\n- Removed DllImport for libvlc_unity_get_texture in TextureHelper\n- Removed VLCUnityStubs.cs (GetTexture is now built-in)\n- VLCMediaPlayer uses new MediaPlayer(LibVLC) directly\n- TextureHelper uses player.GetTexture() directly\n\nBuild with: dotnet build src/LibVLCSharp/LibVLCSharp.csproj -c Release -f netstandard2.1 -p:DefineConstants=\"UNITY DESKTOP\"\n\n* debug(vlc): add logging for texture creation and media player initialization\n\nLogs NativeReference, GetTexture results (width/height/updated/texptr),\nand timeout fallback state to help diagnose why VLC texture is not created.\n\n* fix(vlc): plumb VLC texture directly into TextureManager for display\n\n- BackgroundManager.LoadVideoBackground: set up video texture from\n  TextureManager and display via _venueOutput RawImage for fullscreen\n  display when no venue is present\n- VLCMediaPlayer: add SetExternalOutputTexture to write directly to\n  an external RenderTexture instead of creating internal OutputTexture\n- YargVideoPlayer: pass targetTexture to VLC via SetExternalOutputTexture,\n  remove Graphics.Blit from Update loop\n- OnLoad: conditional VLC_PLUGIN_PATH (check dir exists first)\n- Fix premature timeout: only check VLC prepare timeout after Prepare()\n  has been called (_prepareCalled flag)\n\n* fix(vlc): flip video vertically for OpenGL texture coordinates\n\n* fix(vlc): also flip horizontally to correct mirroring\n\n* fix(vlc): resize target texture to match VLC video dimensions\n\nOnVLCTextureResized now resizes the external RenderTexture to match\nVLC's native video resolution instead of downscaling via Graphics.Blit\n\n* chore(vlc): update NuGet config and packages for LibVLCSharp dependency\n\n* chore(vlc): include VLC native binaries and LibVLCSharp DLL for branch testability\n\nNOTE: These binaries are not intended for production distribution.\nThey are included so developers can test the VLC integration on this branch.\nIn production, LibVLCSharp should be built from source and VLC native binaries\nshould be provided separately.\n\n Please enter the commit message for your changes. Lines starting\n\n* refactor(vlc): replace copied VLC files with git submodules\n\n- Replace manually copied vlc-unity C# files with git submodule\n  (Assets/VLCUnity -> videolan/vlc-unity repo)\n- Replace LibVLCSharp NuGet package with git submodule\n  (Assets/LibVLCSharp -> videolan/libvlcsharp repo)\n- Custom modifications (SetExternalOutputTexture, flip, debug logging,\n  conditional VLC_PLUGIN_PATH) copied into submodule files\n- LibVLCSharp DLL built from source with UNITY DESKTOP symbols\n- Updated Assembly-CSharp.csproj to reference submodule paths\n- Removed Assets/Packages/LibVLCSharp.Unity (no longer needed)\n- Removed Assets/_Recovery and ProfileAnalyzer from git tracking\n\n* remove submods\n\n* Add submodules\n\n* Add vlcunity to assets\n\n* Add script to build libvlcsharp\n\n* Add libVLCUnityPlugin linux binary\n\n* re-add vlcunity differently\n\n* Add libvlcsharp assembly\n\n* wip\n\n* wip\n\n* Proper libvlcsharp\n\n* Plumb video player through\n\n* Fix video start sync for vlc\n\n* Plumb through seeked notification\n\n* Disable audio on vlc player\n\n* Cleanup and fix fallback to unity video player\n\n* Remove spurious meta file\n\n* Complile out vlc support when building for windows\n\nBreaks the build on build fleet, have no way of testing it.\nSomeone who uses windows will need to look at that.\nUntil then just compile it out\n\n* Update Assets/Script/Gameplay/BackgroundManager.cs\n\n* Address PR feedback\n\n* ONLY enable vlc on linux\n\n* fix(vlc): address PR feedback\n\n- restrict libVLCUnityPlugin.so to Linux64 + Linux editor\n- use YargLogger instead of Debug.Log in YargVideoPlayer\n- revert accidental UI position change in Gameplay scene\n- add build notes for LibVLCSharp and native plugin (vlc/BUILDING.md)\n\n* fix(vlc): remove unused private fields in YargVideoPlayer"
